  "id": "tonality",
  "term": "tonality",
  "definition": "Tonality is the way tones in a piece of music are organized around a shared main tone, often called the tonic. In psychology of music, it refers to a complex perceptual skill in which listeners gradually internalize the tonal rules of their musical culture during childhood.",
